 "readme": {
  "file": "README.md",
  "title": "Erdős Problem 1017: clique partitions of graphs of given size",
  "excerpt": "This Lean 4 project concerns [Erdős Problem 1017](https://www.erdosproblems.com/1017), as cataloged by Thomas F. Bloom. Let `f(n, k)` be the least number such that the edges of every graph with `n` vertices and `k` edges can be partitioned into at most `f(n, k)` cliques, a single edge counting as a clique. Erdős, Goodman and Pósa proved `f(n, k) ≤ ⌊n²/4⌋`, which the complete balanced bipartite graph attains. Erdős asked whether this bound can be sharpened when `k > n²/4`, and Bloom's catalog asks for an estimate of `f(n, k)` there."
 },
